{"id": "22526", "revid": "2253620", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=22526", "title": "Misato (Akita)", "text": "Misato (\u7f8e\u90f7\u753a) is a town in Akita prefecture.\nUnderstand.\nThere are three towns with the same name in Japan: the other two are in Shimane and Miyazaki. In addition, some other municipalities are named Misato with other kanjis (\u4e09\u90f7,\n\u7f8e\u91cc, \u4e09\u91cc).\nGet in.\nMisato is east of Yokote and south of Daisen. It is bordered on the east by Iwate."}
{"id": "22527", "revid": "160739", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=22527", "title": "Misato (Kumamoto)", "text": "Misato (\u7f8e\u91cc) is a town in central Kumamoto Prefecture, in Japan.\nUnderstand.\nMisato is a new town created through the combination of two other towns, Chuo and Tomochi. It takes about 40 minutes from Kumamoto City to reach Misato.\nThe area is 144.03 square kilometers and forest covers three quarters of the town."}
